Application forms
=================

Seam: partial application, over-application through apply, a symbol as a
function value, the arity and class checks of the typed boundary.  Memo:
A1, A4.  Catalogue: P10, P44 (the hint of the DefaultingError fits a
module, not a Python call); the relation of example 24.  Issues: none.
Output: map inc [1, 2] is [2, 3]; typeof inc is Int -> Int.  rule 'a' is
a partial application of type [[Char]] -> [Char], and map applies it to
two inputs.  id inc 1 prints as apply (id inc) 1 and is 2: the surplus
argument goes through apply because the result of id inc is a function.
inc 1 2 is an ArityError.  show alone is a DefaultingError with the three
lines of the REPL's sentence; show 1 is '1' because Num a defaults to Int.
rule 'a' ['x'] is cmd1, and usesRel rule, the relation passed as a value,
is cmd2.
Oracle: oracle.out holds the PAKCS 3.4.1 transcripts of the goals over
the module App; the REPL prints the same sentence for show alone.
Backends: py and cxx, one output.
